## 13. Acceptance criteria (testable)

- `npm run build` and `npm run lint` finish with zero errors, and the browser console shows zero errors and warnings on every route.
- Vitest passes for: the engine (golden-path numbers, scenario fixture, scorer returning null when all routes fail, baseline equals analysis output), CSV export (formula-injection guard), and CSV import (valid file, missing column, duplicate IDs, oversized file, malformed quotes).
- Export then import round trip: exporting from History and importing the same file skips all rows as duplicates, and importing it after "Remove imported records" plus a reset restores nothing unexpected.
- Imported records show "User-imported (unverified)", never show simulated values, and never use the Demo tag.
- No horizontal overflow at 375px, 768px, and 1280px.
- A keyboard-only user can create a shipment, run an analysis, open the results page, and open the file picker on the Import Chest (it shows a visible focus ring and opens the lid on focus).
- With `prefers-reduced-motion` on, the AttentiveFace and all other loops are static, and the chest lid still opens and closes without animation.
- With the network disabled, the app loads, the map shows its fallback, and every flow still works.
- Reloading the page keeps shipments, drafts, and imports. Reset demo data restores the seeds.
- A manual grep finds no occurrence of "safe" or "safest" in user-facing strings other than the tagline and negations, and no result is shown without the provenance banner or a tag.
- Every nav item, button, row, and link leads somewhere or does something. Invalid shipment IDs show the not-found state.
- Lighthouse accessibility score of 90 or higher on Dashboard, Create Shipment, Route Analysis, and History.

