# Appendix A: AttentiveFace (animated empty and error states)

**Where:** empty states (no shipments, no search results, empty picker), error states, and the not-found page. Nowhere else. Size 140 to 180px. Always accompany it with a text message, because the face is decoration (`aria-hidden="true"` on the SVG).

**Component:** `components/common/AttentiveFace.jsx` renders:

```jsx
<div className="cc-face-wrap">
  <svg className="face" viewBox="0 0 320 380" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
       strokeWidth="22" strokeLinecap="round" strokeLinejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <g className="face__eyes">
      <g transform="translate(105 120)">
        <path className="face__eye-lid" d="M-26 -22h52" />
        <path className="face__pupil" d="M0 -6v35" pathLength="35" strokeDasharray="35" />
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(215 120)">
        <path className="face__eye-lid" d="M-26 -22h52" />
        <path className="face__pupil" d="M0 -6v35" pathLength="35" strokeDasharray="35" />
      </g>
    </g>
    <path className="face__nose" d="M160 150v38h-16" />
    <path className="face__mouth-left" d="M160 290C140 308 112 308 92 282" pathLength="102" strokeDasharray="102" />
    <path className="face__mouth-right" d="M160 290C180 308 208 308 228 282" pathLength="102" strokeDasharray="102" />
  </svg>
</div>
```

This SVG is a starting skeleton built to match the class names and numbers in the CSS below (pupil dash length 35, mouth dash length 102 via `pathLength`). Render it, look at it, and adjust the path coordinates until it reads as a friendly face whose eyes rise into place, whose nose and smile draw in, whose pupils glance left and blink every 4 seconds. If parts appear outside the face, set `overflow: hidden` on the SVG. Keep the class names unchanged.

